@180  = ~Short Sword~
@181  = ~Bertoxxulous~
@182  = ~The short sword is the first type of sword to come into existence. In the simplest of terms, a short sword can be considered a dagger with a blade so long that it can no longer be called a dagger. The term short sword does not exist in sword classifications. However, it has come to be used to describe a double-edged blade about two feet in length. The sword tip is usually pointed, ideal for thrusting.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1D6
Damage type: piercing
Weight: 3
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Short Sword
Type: 1-handed
Requires: 5 Strength
Not Usable By:
 Druid
 Cleric
 Mage
 Beast Master~
@183  = ~Bertoxxulous, The Plaguebringer

"The only truth is that everyone dies." is printed upon the blade near the hilt in a demonic tongue. While holding this sword the weilder views the decay of flesh as a thing of ultimate beauty. The subtle purples of a fresh bruise, the almost iridescent yellow green of infested pustule, are but a few of the things the weilder begins to relish.
The sword glows with a black icor when magic is used to reveal it's nature. Necromancy's evil infests every part of the weapon. Those who would use such a foul sword, for them there is nothing more desirable than to be surrounded by beings who, even in unlife, continue to rot and decay.
Not much else can be learned about this sword other than it's origins come from the Nine Hells.

STATISTICS:

Ability 1: Target struck suffers a -3 to their movement for 60 seconds if a save vs. wands is not made.
Ability 2: Target struck suffers a -2 to their dexterity for 30 seconds with no saving throw.
Ability 3: Target struck suffers 5 poison damage over 2 secs unless a save vs. poison/death magic is made.

Penalty 1: -1 Constitution.
Penalty 2: Cursed.

THAC0: +6
Damage: 1D6 +6
Damage type: piercing
Weight: 2
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Short Sword
Type: 1-handed

Usable By:
 Evil Aligned Characters~
@184  = ~Spear~
@185  = ~Prexus~
@186  = ~One of man's earliest weapons, dating back to the most primitive of times, the first spears were simply wooden poles or sticks sharpened at one end. When man mastered metals, spearheads were made from iron and steel. Having reached this end, weaponers began experimenting with different types of spear heads, thus leading to the development of certain polearm types.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1D6
Damage type: piercing
